# Runtime config — this project's ".env" equivalent (see env.js/
# env.example.js's own doc comments). Deliberately left OUT of
# .gitignore (commented out below): GitHub Pages/Vercel serve this
# repo's files as-is with no build step to inject env.js's values at
# deploy time, so it has to be committed for the deployed site to work.
# Safe to commit — it only ever holds the public anon key, never the
# service_role key. See env.js's own doc comment for the full reasoning.
